course: dictionary
lesson: 2318
title: Crossing: a place, a trip, or an action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word crossing can mean different things. Look at the words around it to find out which one is meant. «Children can find it hard to judge how fast a car is coming, which is one more reason to cross at a crossing.» The first crossing is a place: a safe spot on a road. The second word, cross, is a verb: it means to go across.
explain: «A fast train can need over a kilometre to stop, which is why level crossings have barriers.» A level crossing is a place where a road and a railway meet, so the words around it, train and barriers, help you know it is a place. Always ask: what does this word do in the sentence? A noun names a thing, and a verb shows an action.
explain: Crossing can also mean a trip over water. «The ferry crossing to the island takes twenty minutes.» Here the ferry is a boat, and the island is across the water, so a crossing is a trip across water. Try your meaning in the sentence: does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: A crossing is a place where you can go across a road, a river or a railway safely.
fact: A crossing can also be a trip across water, like a ferry crossing.
fact: Crossing is also a verb, from cross: «crossing the road» means going across the road.
fact: «Pedestrian crossing», «zebra crossing», «level crossing», «crossing guard» and «border crossing» are all phrases using crossing as a noun.
fact: A crossing guard helps children cross the road safely.
exercise: «Children can find it hard to judge how fast a car is coming, which is one more reason to cross at a crossing.» What is a crossing in this sentence? | A trip across the sea on a boat | A kind of car that goes very fast | *A safe place to go across a road | A rope bridge over a stream
exercise: «A fast train can need over a kilometre to stop, which is why level crossings have barriers.» What is a level crossing? | *A place where a road and a railway meet, with barriers | A train station with a big clock | A flat piece of ground for football | A steep hill with a narrow path
exercise: In «crossing the road», what does crossing mean? | Shouting loudly | Standing still | Looking for a bus | *Going across
test: The ferry crossing to the island takes twenty minutes. What is a ferry crossing? | A kind of bicycle lane | A road for cars only | Stop for buses on the high street | *A trip across water by boat
test: The crossing guard waved the children over the road. What does a crossing guard do? | To mend the railway barriers | To sell tickets on the ferry | *To help children cross the road safely | To drive the school bus
exam: A zebra crossing is a safe place to go across a road. What does zebra crossing mean? | *A safe place with stripes where people can cross a road | A kind of bus stop | A striped zebra at the zoo | A road that goes only one way
